# kcov.config — DISCOVERY-ONLY, NON-CONFORMING for validation
#
# Profile:        kcov (coverage-guided discovery — PRIMARY for triage)
# Kbase:          r54p0-01eac0 (primary)  [+ patches/virtual-device/ 0001-0006]
# Kernel:         UNKNOWN — not selected. ARM GUIDANCE: latest ACK or latest
#                 Linux stable/LTS (research/program-scope.md §4)
# Patch set:      vendor/virtual-device 0001-0006, PLUS a future research patch
#                 in kernel/patches/ for Kbase-side coverage (not yet written)
# Scope class:    DISCOVERY-ONLY / NON-CONFORMING FOR VALIDATION
#                 CONFIG_KCOV and CONFIG_KCOV_INSTRUMENT_ALL are NOT on the Arm
#                 kernel allowlist (program-scope.md §5). Also, the whole x86
#                 NO_MALI harness is investigation-only (DECISION-1, §8.5).
#                 Usable to FIND bugs; never a conforming validation environment.
#                 Findings here must be re-confirmed on a conforming config
#                 before they mean anything (program-scope.md §6).
# Generated from: Arm's virtual-platform guide Kbase options + Linux KCOV symbols
#                 named from general mainline knowledge (NOT verified against any
#                 kernel, because none is chosen).
# Validation:     PROVISIONAL — never fed to a build. Full config UNKNOWN.
# Config hash:    N/A (placeholder fragment; no real .config has been produced)
#
# NOT a valid .config. NOT the output of make defconfig/savedefconfig.

# Purpose: coverage-guided discovery. This is the profile that drives the primary
# fuzzing triage loop, and it is INTENTIONALLY non-conforming — see Scope class
# above and project spec §13, §16, §24 (F-9).

# --- Kbase driver options, verbatim from Arm's virtual-platform guide ------
CONFIG_MALI_MIDGARD=m
CONFIG_MALI_CSF_SUPPORT=y
CONFIG_MALI_EXPERT=y
CONFIG_MALI_DEBUG=n
CONFIG_MALI_NO_MALI=y
# CONFIG_MALI_REAL_HW is not set
# Latest GPU target defined by r54p0 (DECISION-2); investigation-only.
CONFIG_MALI_NO_MALI_DEFAULT_GPU="tDRx"
CONFIG_MALI_PLATFORM_NAME="vexpress"

# --- Kbase-side coverage: DELIBERATELY ABSENT, AND UNAVAILABLE -------------
# MALI_KCOV is defined only in midgard/Mconfig (the Android/SCons path), not in
# midgard/Kconfig, and its -fsanitize-coverage=trace-cmp flags live only in the
# SCons/Android Makefile an in-tree build never reads. Writing CONFIG_MALI_KCOV
# here would be silently ignored. Closing this gap needs a research patch in
# kernel/patches/ (findings.md F-2). Until that patch exists and is built, this
# profile yields a kernel with KCOV enabled but Kbase itself UNINSTRUMENTED.

# --- Linux coverage subsystem (NOT on the Arm allowlist) -------------------
# These make the KERNEL emit coverage; KCOV is Linux's runtime subsystem,
# independent of MALI_KCOV (which would make Kbase emit it).
CONFIG_KCOV=y
CONFIG_KCOV_INSTRUMENT_ALL=y

# --- Kernel hard build gates, set explicitly ------------------------------
# VERIFIED: midgard/Kbuild:29-39 raises $(error ...) for these; test is `=n` and
# does not catch unset. Expected to be default y (NO-OP delta) but to be
# CONFIRMED by savedefconfig diff. See findings.md F-3.
CONFIG_DMA_SHARED_BUFFER=y
CONFIG_PM_DEVFREQ=y
CONFIG_DEVFREQ_THERMAL=y

# --- UNRESOLVED, for the build phase --------------------------------------
# - Exact kernel version.
# - Whether the Kbase-side coverage research patch is needed and sufficient.
# - Full minimal configuration.